== Tips ==
*While the boss does {{stat|tdmg}} its demons deal high amount of regular {{stat|dmg}}, therefore prioritizing one over the other too much will not work against the Slayer.
*If the player can deal high and rapid damage, the slayer boss will not be able to throw any fire pillars before the split or death. Damage nullification items like {{Item|Spirit Mask}} or Phoenix Pet should be prepared in case the player fails to deal enough damage in time or fails to breaking pillar.
**Due to the Hellion Shield mitigation of [[Venomous]] damage, the [[One For All]] ultimate enchant will prove to be the highest DPS option for many players, heavily assisting in the "DPS-Race" style of this slayer.
*Using {{Item|Opal Gemstone}} on combat slots of armor and daggers can help massively for nullifying the {{stat|tdmg}} boss deals, if more survivability is needed.
*When boss uses DDR-Apocalypse ability, blocks that will be lit will be marked on the ground, so make sure to avoid marked blocks.

== Trivia ==
* Because of vanilla Minecraft AI and abilities, Typhoeus is stronger than Quazii. Therefore, the [[Firedust Dagger]], [[Kindlebane Dagger]] and [[Pyrochaos Dagger]] are respectively stronger than the [[Twilight Dagger]], [[Mawdredge Dagger]] and [[Deathripper Dagger]] if the Burning Vengeance ﬗ ability is counted.
* If both Quazii and Typhoeus spawn in a place which is one block large and get pushed, Quazii always gets pushed into the wall and take suffocation damage first.
* Contrary to its description, the '''DDR Apocalypse''' fire's damage is based on the player's current {{Stat|HP}}, not their max {{Stat|HP}}.
* Despite being classified as {{stat|tdmg}}, the damage of the demons' '''ROFLcopter''' and '''Trail of Fire''' is unaffected by {{stat|true defense}}.

